node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
.DS_Store

# env
#
# Deliberately broad. `.env*.local` only matches names ENDING in .local, so a
# `.env.local.bak` written by an editor, a script, or a careful person about to
# change something was committable, and it holds every key the project has. One
# rule that covers every variant, with the template explicitly exempted.
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# Reference images for the column illustration.
#
# Staged here, pushed to R2, and served from there. Deliberately not committed:
# they are binaries that would bloat every clone forever, and the bucket is
# already the place this project serves images from. The manifest that names them
# IS committed, in src/lib/ai/image-refs.ts, so the repo still records what the
# set is meant to contain even though it does not carry the bytes.
assets/refs/**
!assets/refs/README.md
# The pose labels are text, cost a vision request each to work out, and are the
# record of which render is a run and which is a crouch. Worth keeping.
!assets/refs/poses.json
